__d(function(g,r,i,a,m,e,d){"use strict";Object.defineProperty(e,'__esModule',{value:!0}),Object.defineProperty(e,"LEGAL_VERSION",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return o}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"ENTITY_PENDING",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return t}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"MIN_AGE",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return n}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"COMPANY",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return s}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"TERMS",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return c}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"PRIVACY",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return l}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"ATTRIBUTIONS",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return u}});const o='2026-10-09',t=!0,n=18,s={name:'NitoPath',publisher:'NitoPath',contactEmail:'Nitopath@gmail.com',jurisdiction:'the United States',website:'https://nitopath.com'},c={title:'Terms of Service',updated:o,intro:[`These terms are an agreement between you and ${s.name} ("we", "us") covering your use of the NitoPath app and related services (the "Service").`,'By tapping to accept, creating an account, or using the Service, you agree to these terms. If you do not agree, do not use the Service.'],sections:[{heading:'1. Who may use NitoPath',body:[`You must be at least ${n} years old to use the Service. The Service is not directed to children and we do not knowingly collect information from anyone under ${n}.`,'If you use the Service while operating a vehicle, you must hold a valid driver licence and carry any insurance the law requires where you drive.','You may not use the Service if the law where you are prohibits it, or if we have previously suspended your account.']},{heading:'2. What NitoPath is \u2014 and is not',body:['NitoPath is an informational navigation aid. It shows the locations of automated licence plate readers (ALPRs) that volunteers have recorded in OpenStreetMap, and it can plan driving routes that pass fewer of them or that pass more of them, whichever you choose. People use it in both directions: some prefer fewer cameras, others prefer to travel on monitored roads.','Camera data is crowdsourced and is always incomplete, and it may be wrong, outdated, or missing entirely. A route the app describes as having no known cameras may still pass cameras that nobody has mapped, cameras that were installed recently, or mobile and temporary cameras. Surveillance may also occur through means the app knows nothing about.','Whichever mode you use, the Service does not make you anonymous, does not prevent you from being recorded, photographed or identified, does not defeat any surveillance system, and does not make any route safe. Do not rely on it for safety, for privacy, or for any legal purpose.','Routes, distances, travel times and arrival estimates are estimates only. Roads, closures, traffic, construction and restrictions change constantly and the Service will not always know about them.']},{heading:'3. Safe driving is your responsibility',body:['Always obey traffic laws, road signs, signals, speed limits, and the instructions of law enforcement and road crews. Real-world conditions and posted signs always take priority over anything the app shows or says.','Do not type, read, or interact with the app while driving. Set your destination before you start moving, or have a passenger do it. Use voice guidance and keep your eyes on the road.','The Service may direct you onto routes that are longer, slower, unlit, unpaved, unfamiliar, restricted, or unsuitable for your vehicle. You are solely responsible for deciding whether a route is safe and lawful for you to drive.','You accept all risk arising from your driving and your use of the Service.']},{heading:'4. Lawful use only',body:['You agree to use the Service only for lawful purposes. You may not use it to evade, obstruct or interfere with law enforcement, to commit or conceal any crime, to flee the scene of an incident, or to avoid a lawful order, warrant, summons, court order, or any legal obligation.','You may not use the Service to follow, locate, harass, stalk, intimidate or endanger any person, or to interfere with, damage, disable, obstruct or tamper with any camera, sensor or other equipment.','You may not trespass, enter restricted areas, or break any law in order to observe or record camera locations.','You may not scrape, bulk-download, resell or redistribute data from the Service except as the underlying data licences allow; reverse engineer or tamper with the app or our servers; attempt to access data belonging to other users; or use automated means to overload or abuse the Service.']},{heading:'5. Accounts',body:['An account is optional. Without one you can still plan routes and receive alerts; an account adds saved places, saved routes, trip history and settings that follow you between devices.','Keep your password confidential. You are responsible for activity under your account. Tell us promptly if you believe it has been compromised.','You can delete your account at any time from within the app, which permanently removes your account data.','We may suspend or terminate accounts that breach these terms, that create legal risk for us or others, or where we are required to do so.']},{heading:'6. Camera reports you submit',body:['If you report a camera, you confirm that you personally observed it, that your report is accurate to the best of your knowledge, and that you gathered the information lawfully and safely.','Do not submit reports about private individuals, personal information, or anything that is not a publicly visible piece of surveillance equipment.','You grant us a worldwide, non-exclusive, royalty-free licence to store, reproduce, modify, publish and distribute your reports as part of the Service, including contributing them to open data projects such as OpenStreetMap under those projects\' licences. You keep whatever rights you had in the content.','We may review, edit, reject or remove any report at our discretion. Reports may be visible to other users once approved.']},{heading:'7. Our app, and what you may not do with it',body:[`NitoPath \u2014 its name, logo, design, screens, layout, wording, graphics, code, server logic and the methods it uses to plan routes \u2014 belongs to ${s.name} or its licensors, and is protected by copyright, trademark and other laws. Using the Service gives you no ownership of any of it.`,'You get a personal, limited, non-exclusive, non-transferable, revocable licence to use the app on devices you control, for your own use. Everything not expressly granted is reserved.','You may not copy, reproduce, adapt, translate or create derivative works from the app or any part of it; reverse engineer, decompile or disassemble it, or otherwise try to discover its source code or how its server-side features work, except to the extent the law expressly permits despite this restriction; remove or obscure any notice of ownership; rent, lease, sell, sublicense or redistribute it; or scrape, harvest or bulk-extract its screens, content or data.','You may not use the Service, or anything you take from it, to build, design or operate a product or service that competes with NitoPath, or to help anyone else do so. That includes copying its screens, flows, wording, graphics, icons or the specific way its features behave, and includes using its output to train machine learning models.','Camera locations come from OpenStreetMap and are open data under the ODbL. That data is not ours, and nothing in this section restricts the rights that licence gives you in it. What is ours is this app: its software, its design, and the way it works.']},{heading:'8. Third-party data and services',body:['Camera locations come from OpenStreetMap contributors and are licensed under the Open Database License (ODbL). Map display uses Google Maps on Android and Apple Maps on iOS, and is subject to Google\'s or Apple\'s terms respectively. Routing and address search use openrouteservice (HeiGIT) and, as a fallback, Photon by Komoot and OSRM.','Your use of those parts of the Service is also subject to those providers\' terms and privacy policies. We do not control them and are not responsible for their content, availability or accuracy.','The Service depends on these free and community services. They can be slow, rate-limited, or unavailable, and features may stop working without notice.']},{heading:'9. The Service is provided "as is"',body:['To the fullest extent the law allows, the Service is provided as is and as available, without warranties of any kind, whether express, implied or statutory, including any implied warranties of merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, accuracy, or non-infringement.','We do not warrant that the Service will be uninterrupted, timely, secure, accurate, complete, or error-free, or that camera data reflects reality at any moment.']},{heading:'10. Limitation of liability',body:[`To the fullest extent the law allows, neither ${s.name} nor anyone involved in creating or delivering the Service is liable for any indirect, incidental, special, consequential, exemplary or punitive damages, or for any loss of profits, data, goodwill, or for personal injury, death, property damage, vehicle collision, traffic citation, arrest, prosecution, fine, or any other loss arising out of or relating to your use of, or inability to use, the Service.`,"Our total liability for all claims relating to the Service is limited to the greater of the amount you paid us in the twelve months before the claim, or twenty-five US dollars (US$25).",'Some places do not allow the exclusion of certain warranties or the limitation of certain damages, so parts of this section may not apply to you. Nothing in these terms limits liability that cannot be limited by law, including for fraud, or for death or personal injury caused by negligence where that limitation is prohibited.']},{heading:'11. Indemnity',body:[`You agree to indemnify and hold harmless ${s.name} and its officers, employees and contractors from any claim, demand, loss, liability, or expense (including reasonable legal fees) arising from your use of the Service, your breach of these terms, your violation of any law, or your infringement of anyone's rights.`]},{heading:'12. Changes',body:['We may change the Service or these terms. If we make a material change to these terms we will ask you to accept the new version in the app. Continuing to use the Service after that means you accept the change.','We may add, change, limit or remove features, including paid features, at any time.']},{heading:'13. Ending this agreement',body:['You may stop using the Service and delete your account at any time. We may suspend or end your access if you breach these terms.','Sections that by their nature should survive termination \u2014 including lawful use, liability limits, indemnity and governing law \u2014 survive.']},{heading:'14. Governing law and disputes',body:[`These terms are governed by the laws of ${s.jurisdiction}, without regard to conflict-of-laws rules. Courts located in ${s.jurisdiction} have exclusive jurisdiction, and you and we consent to their jurisdiction and venue.`,'Nothing here removes any right you have to bring a claim in your local courts where the law gives you that right.']},{heading:'15. Contact',body:[`Questions about these terms: ${s.contactEmail}`]}]},l={title:'Privacy Policy',updated:o,intro:[`This policy explains what ${s.name} collects when you use NitoPath, why, who else sees it, and what control you have.`,'Short version: the app works without an account and we keep as little as we can. We do not sell your personal information and we do not use it for advertising.'],sections:[{heading:'Location',body:['Your device location is used to centre the map, to plan routes from where you are, and to warn you about nearby cameras. Camera alerts are calculated on your phone.','When you plan a route or search for an address, the start, destination and search text are sent to our servers and on to our routing and search providers (openrouteservice, and Photon or OSRM as fallbacks) so they can return a route or results. Those requests are not tied to your account.','We do not track your location in the background outside a trip. The app only asks for permission to use location while you are using it, and you can revoke that permission in your phone\'s settings at any time.','During a trip or in Drive mode, NitoPath keeps receiving your location if the phone locks or you switch to another app, so directions and camera alerts continue. Your phone shows this (a location indicator on iPhone, a notification on Android), and it stops when the trip or Drive mode ends. These positions are used on your phone only and are not uploaded. You can turn this off in Settings under "Guide with the screen locked".','The camera log (a count of the known cameras you have driven past, with dates) is worked out and stored on your phone only. It is never uploaded or synced to your account. You can turn it off or clear it under Camera log, and deleting the app deletes it.','Your continuous location trail is never uploaded. If you are signed in and you start a trip, we store a record of that trip (start, destination, distance, duration, camera counts) in your history, which you can delete.']},{heading:'Account information',body:['If you create an account we store your email address, a password (hashed, never in readable form), and an optional display name.','With an account we also store your settings, saved places (such as home and work), saved routes, and trip history \u2014 so they follow you between devices.','Without an account, settings and recent searches stay on your phone only.']},{heading:'Camera reports',body:['If you report a camera we store the coordinates you reported, any note you add, the direction you selected, and your account ID so we can review it and so you can withdraw it.','Approved reports may become part of the shared camera map, and may be contributed to OpenStreetMap, where they become public open data. Do not include personal information in report notes.']},{heading:'Technical data',body:['Our servers keep short-lived logs containing request details such as IP address, timestamps and error messages. These are used to keep the service running and to investigate abuse, and are kept only as long as needed for that.','The app stores data on your device (settings, recent searches, your login session) using your phone\'s own storage.']},{heading:'Who processes your data',body:['Supabase \u2014 hosting, database and authentication (servers in the United States).','Google Maps SDK for Android \u2014 displays the map on Android. Google receives map usage data directly under its own privacy policy.','Apple Maps (MapKit) \u2014 displays the map on iOS. Apple receives map usage data directly under its own privacy policy.','openrouteservice (HeiGIT, Germany) \u2014 routing and address search. Receives the coordinates and search text needed to answer a request.','Photon by Komoot and the OSRM demo service \u2014 fallbacks when the above is unavailable.','OpenStreetMap Overpass servers \u2014 our servers download camera locations by geographic region. These requests come from our servers and contain no user data.','We do not sell personal information, we do not share it with data brokers, and we do not use it for advertising or profiling.']},{heading:'Legal requests',body:['We will only disclose personal information if we are legally required to, and we will resist requests we believe are invalid or overbroad, to the extent the law allows.','Keep in mind that we cannot hand over what we never collected: without an account, we hold no profile of you, and we never store your continuous location trail.']},{heading:'Keeping data and deleting it',body:['Account data is kept while your account exists. Deleting your account in the app (Account \u2192 Delete account) permanently removes your profile, settings, saved places, saved routes, trip history and reports.','You can clear trip history and recent searches separately at any time in the app.',`If you cannot access the app, you can request deletion by emailing ${s.contactEmail} from the address on the account.`,'Backups may retain copies for a short period before being overwritten.']},{heading:'Security',body:['Traffic between the app and our servers is encrypted in transit. Database access is restricted by per-user security rules, so one account cannot read another account\'s data.','No service is perfectly secure. Use a strong, unique password.']},{heading:'Your rights',body:['You can access, correct, export or delete your data. Most of this is available directly in the app; for anything else, contact us.',`Depending on where you live, you may have additional rights under laws such as the GDPR or the CCPA, including the right to object to processing or to complain to a regulator. We do not sell or share personal information as those laws define it. To exercise any right, contact ${s.contactEmail}.`]},{heading:'Children',body:[`The Service is for people aged ${n} and over. We do not knowingly collect data from children. If you believe a child has given us information, contact us and we will delete it.`]},{heading:'Changes and contact',body:['If we make a significant change to this policy we will ask you to review it in the app.',`Questions, requests or complaints: ${s.contactEmail}`]}]},u=['Camera locations \xa9 OpenStreetMap contributors, licensed under the Open Database License (ODbL), largely mapped by the DeFlock community.','Routing and address search powered by openrouteservice, with OSRM and Photon by Komoot as fallbacks.','Map tiles and display by Google Maps on Android and Apple Maps on iOS.','In the web app, map tiles by OpenFreeMap using OpenMapTiles and \xa9 OpenStreetMap contributors, drawn with MapLibre.']},1463,[]);
